Done. Summary of this executor slice (US-135, M10a-3, `partial`):

**Implemented** — workspace BYOK is now consumed at generation time:
- `AiModelRegistryService.runWithWorkspaceRegistry(workspaceId, fn)` installs a request-scoped `AsyncLocalStorage` view built from the workspace-resolved providers; all read accessors use the active view. No global maps are mutated.
- Workspace SDK instances are built with `createTransientProvider` (the providerName-keyed cache would leak workspace A's key to B), and `RegisteredAiModel.rawProvider` is carried so native tools bind to the same BYOK provider.
- `ProviderConfigService.getWorkspaceProviderResolution` returns `{ providers, hasWorkspaceOverrides }`; key-less workspaces keep the exact prior instance path.
- Wired generation call sites: chat, agent executor, generate-text REST, title generation, turn grader, setup-chat, and chat-resolver availability.

**Checks (all green, Tier 0):** `tsgo --noEmit` exit 0; new registry + provider-config specs 12 passed; `--findRelatedTests` 22 suites / 163 passed; oxlint 0/0; oxfmt clean; no `locales/**` churn; no AI attribution.

